# ---- Local working state (never leaves this machine) ----------------------
# Development snapshots. Large, machine-local, and deliberately kept on disk.
_snapshots/
_snapshots.7z
*.7z

# Per-machine runtime state: port cache, your preferences, the pickle-trust
# allowlist. Regenerated on demand; committing it would leak local config and
# churn on every run.
.mpynode_local/

# Agent / editor local settings
.claude/
.superpowers/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
build/lib/
dist/

# ---- Compiled Maya plug-ins ------------------------------------------------
# NO binaries ship. A Maya plug-in is built against one Maya version's devkit
# and will not load in another, so shipping one would be shipping something
# most users cannot use. The .cpp sources and the full optimizer step lineage
# under templates/**/build/stages/ ARE committed, so every binary is
# reproducible on the user's own machine:
#   one template -- bash "templates/<Family>/<Name>/build/build.sh" [maya-version]
#   all in one   -- bash "templates/All Templates Plugin/build.sh" [maya-version]
#                   (build.bat on Windows)
# tools/build_compiled_templates.sh REGENERATES the C++ from the .mpn sources
# (transpile + AI assist + optimizer, hours, needs mayapy and the Claude CLI).
# It is not the way to compile what is already committed.
*.bundle
*.so
*.mll
*.pyd
*.o
*.obj
*.dylib
# MSVC-only link byproducts. `cl /LD` used to write <first-obj>.lib + .exp
# into the CWD, not the output dir, so building or running the suite from the
# repo root littered it -- 29 such files after one mega build plus one test
# run. Since 2026-09-08 the cmd builders and every build.bat pin them beside
# the plugin (/IMPLIB, /Fo) and delete them after the link; the rule stays
# for anything built by hand. clang emits neither. No tracked file in the
# project ends in .lib or .exp.
*.lib
*.exp

# ---- Build scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
# _audit/ is where tools/harness/run_all*.py write per-template audit output.
# It is deliberately NOT under templates/: those folders are keyed on a FLAT
# name (MPyBlendShape_Combo_Correctives), so writing them there would scatter
# fake node families through the tree users are told to browse.
_audit/
_optscratch/
_runner/
compile.log
**/build/_optscratch/
*.bak
*.orig

# ---- Local launchers / machine state ---------------------------------------
# Developer-machine conveniences and per-run state. They are useful locally but
# are specific to one install, so they are never part of what ships.
/LaunchMaya2026.app/
/launch_maya2024.sh
/launch_maya2025.bat
/userSetup.py
.bench.lock

# ---- OS / editor junk ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.swp

# ---- Maya ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Hypershade swatch cache Maya drops beside a scene or texture it previewed.
.mayaSwatches/
